{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal would provide self-contained residential unit within the curtilage of existing property, that would be in conflict with other Local Plan policies. The proposal would be unacceptable in principle and would fail to comply with Local Plan policy SC1 (Housing Growth).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development would introduce a self-contained unit into the rear garden of an existing property, an incongruous addition to the site and surrounding area, harmful to the character and appearance of the host property and wider area contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development would create an independent planning unit in the garden of an existing property and would result in an increased level of activity, noise and disturbance and loss of privacy to neighbouring properties, harmful to neighbouring properties would be contrary to Local Plan policy CC2.",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposal would fail to provide an acceptable standard of accommodation for the occupiers of Flats 2 and 3 of the host dwelling and the future occupiers of the proposed new dwelling, by reason of inadequate external amenity space. It is therefore contrary to Local Plan policy SC5 and London Plan policy D6.",
    "Reason : 5 - The proposal would result in conditions prejudicial to the free flow and safety of pedestrian and vehicular movements due to the enclosure of the private service road and the lack of a paved footway to access the property from the highway, and the insufficient pedestrian and cycle access arrangements, contrary to London Plan policy T6.1 and Local Plan policy EC2, as well as the Council's adopted Residential Crossover and Off-Street Parking Policy."
  ],
